sentences.l:
Not has warbled at-dawn a grey-dove on a branch * but there stirred in me the killer of grief;
nor has sighed a longing-one in whom is rapture * for the beloved-ones, but my sorrow grew in me.
I complain of love-torment to one who is not pitying me; * how-often has passion parted between the soul and the body!

sentences.i:
No grey dove has ever sung at dawn upon a branch but in me there stirred a grief that kills;
no longing lover, moved to rapture, has ever sighed for those he loves but my sorrow grew within me.
I tell my love's torment to one who has no pity for me. How often has passion parted soul from body!
